Shell Scripting:

1. shell : it is an interface between user and OS

2. Types of shell:
--> sh (Bourn shell)
--> ksh (korn shell)
--> csh (C shell)
--> zsh (z shell)
--> fish 
--> bash 

to check out current shell: $SHELL or $0 
check all system supported shell: /etc/shells file

Shell scritpting:
--> Shell scripting is the process of writing a set of linux commands in afile so that they can execute automatically.

what is shebang line?
--> #!/bin/bash
----> it is used to instruct OS to use bash as a command interpreter
----> shebang refers to # and !. in musical notation # called sharp and ! called bang
----> shebang line specifing the interpreter.

